{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02800",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 7.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Right, you know, sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.14,
      "end_seconds": 13.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.77,
      "end_seconds": 21.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Honestly, it's my heart suddenly racing, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.53,
      "end_seconds": 27.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.03,
      "end_seconds": 50.69,
      "duration_seconds": 19.66,
      "text": "So, honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down. And a pounding in my neck, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.58,
      "end_seconds": 56.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Has there been it stopping just as suddenly too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.47,
      "end_seconds": 59.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Yes, uh, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.65,
      "end_seconds": 71.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Any sign of fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.06,
      "end_seconds": 74.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "No. No fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.32,
      "end_seconds": 87.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chest pain, family history of sudden death or breathlessness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.45,
      "end_seconds": 92.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Right, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.83,
      "end_seconds": 97.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.0,
      "end_seconds": 100.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.92,
      "end_seconds": 104.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.3,
      "end_seconds": 107.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.9,
      "end_seconds": 112.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.45,
      "end_seconds": 136.01,
      "duration_seconds": 22.56,
      "text": "I have an irregular heartbeat, for five years. I just want to get back to normal, really. I took the morning off to come in today. I've had high cholesterol for five years now. I've got heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.51,
      "end_seconds": 141.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.0,
      "end_seconds": 149.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, I'm on metoprolol, twice a day for the heart rhythm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.55,
      "end_seconds": 153.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.87,
      "end_seconds": 162.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "It's 50 milligrams. Oh, you know, it's rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.75,
      "end_seconds": 169.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.7,
      "end_seconds": 182.29,
      "duration_seconds": 11.59,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day. Atorvastatin I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.33,
      "end_seconds": 185.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.5,
      "end_seconds": 190.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.53,
      "end_seconds": 195.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.37,
      "end_seconds": 201.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.83,
      "end_seconds": 205.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Alright, how are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.91,
      "end_seconds": 210.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.57,
      "end_seconds": 214.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.95,
      "end_seconds": 219.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.6,
      "end_seconds": 226.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.24,
      "end_seconds": 233.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Yes, plasters. I get a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.22,
      "end_seconds": 252.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.8,
      "end_seconds": 266.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.46,
      "end_seconds": 285.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 125 over 81, SpO2 98 percent on room air, respiratory rate 17, pulse is 86 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.68,
      "end_seconds": 289.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.64,
      "end_seconds": 294.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.45,
      "end_seconds": 301.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.53,
      "end_seconds": 304.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.26,
      "end_seconds": 315.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.14,
      "end_seconds": 321.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.82,
      "end_seconds": 346.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, this is probably episodes of supraventricular tachycardia. We shouldn't forget atrial fibrillation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.56,
      "end_seconds": 351.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Let me think, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.47,
      "end_seconds": 390.45,
      "duration_seconds": 37.98,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's episodes of supraventricular tachycardia, and we'll know more once the a thyroid test is back. We should do a thyroid test for palpitations. A 7-day heart monitor is what I'd like next, for paroxysmal palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.16,
      "end_seconds": 395.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "So, thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.76,
      "end_seconds": 400.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "We'll catch up after the monitor. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.0,
      "end_seconds": 406.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I mean, good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}